<!--
    Fi3ldMan custom scripts for topic pages, for every publication.

    This replaces the old `topic-page-libraries.xml` + the `whc:page_libraries`
    override in customTopicPage.xsl. That approach hard-coded Oxygen's own asset
    list (commons.css, commons.js, topic.js), which silently broke on the
    Oxygen 2024 -> 2026 upgrade when those bundles were renamed and re-split.

    Oxygen now emits its own assets via <whc:page_css> and <whc:page_libraries>
    in the page layouts; this fragment only adds the four Fi3ldMan scripts on
    top, so it does not need touching when Oxygen changes its bundling.

    gramframe.bundle.js is only used by pub-10, which publishes from this same
    template: it replaces every table carrying outputclass="gram-config" with an
    interactive spectrogram. It loads on pub-5's pages too and is a no-op there -
    its entry point does querySelectorAll("table.gram-config"), finds nothing and
    stops. Loading it unconditionally is deliberate: a second .opt and a second
    fragment existed briefly to keep it off pub-5, and cost 63 lines of
    hand-synchronised duplication to save a script tag that does nothing.

    Injected via the `webhelp.fragment.head.topic.page` placeholder - see the
    <html-fragments> section of f13ldMan.opt.

    The <head> wrapper is ignored - only its children are copied into the output.
-->
<head xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:whc="http://www.oxygenxml.com/webhelp/components" whc:version="28.1">

    <script defer="defer" src="${oxygen-webhelp-assets-dir}/template/resources/current-handler.js?buildId=${oxygen-webhelp-build-number}"></script>
    <script defer="defer" src="${oxygen-webhelp-assets-dir}/template/resources/sorttable.js?buildId=${oxygen-webhelp-build-number}"></script>
    <script defer="defer" src="${oxygen-webhelp-assets-dir}/template/resources/harmonics.js?buildId=${oxygen-webhelp-build-number}"></script>
    <script defer="defer" src="${oxygen-webhelp-assets-dir}/template/resources/gramframe.bundle.js?buildId=${oxygen-webhelp-build-number}"></script>
</head>
